{"id": 31, "ts": 1780458289.4972136, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I agree with the panel that Candidate\u202fC remains the strongest overall fit.\u202fWhile Candidate\u202fA demonstrates impressive technical foresight\u2014he can anticipate dangerous situations, sees complex connections, and has excellent spatial vision, plus very good leadership qualities\u2014there is no evidence of his operational reliability or crew\u2011cooperation, and his difficulty taking criticism and being unorganized raise concerns for the consistency required on long\u2011haul flights.\u202fCandidate\u202fB is very conscientious, handles stress well, and excels at weather assessment and computer use, yet we lack any concrete evidence of his decision\u2011making quality under pressure, and his grumpy, uncooperative demeanor could undermine cockpit teamwork.\u202fCandidate\u202fD shows strong concentration, problem\u2011solving, and a serious sense of responsibility, but his arrogance and relatively weak leadership pose serious risks to crew cooperation and professional communication.\u202fIn contrast, Candidate\u202fC has documented 100\u202f% reliability, makes correct decisions quickly, and creates a positive crew atmosphere\u2014directly satisfying operational reliability, decision quality, and crew\u2011cooperation criteria.\u202fAlthough we have limited evidence of his adaptability and feedback orientation, the core safety\u2011critical strengths outweigh the concerns.\u202fTherefore, I maintain my vote for Candidate\u202fC."}
